  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study focuses on mapping spatial and temporal variations in noise levels but does not analyze the specific technical or vehicular causes behind the elevated decibel readings.",
      "what": "This study measured equivalent, minimum, and maximum A-weighted sound levels in decibels at 27 major traffic intersections across Varanasi, India, during morning, afternoon, and evening hours. The measurements revealed that noise levels at all 27 locations exceeded permissible urban limits throughout the entire day, with the highest noise concentrations recorded at commercial intersections like Pandeypur, Maidagin, and Lanka.",
      "why": "The study establishes that noise pollution in Varanasi is continuous and ubiquitous, proving that even the lowest recorded sound levels in quieter areas exceed recommended safety standards, leaving residents with no period of relief from harmful noise exposure."
